\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Architecture and decision flow of CodeTwin AI. Layer~1 collects evidence about a change, and Layer~2 stores it in a typed dependency graph. Layer~3 calculates a score for each test file and selects tests within a budget or above a threshold calibrated on recent commits; if the estimated residual risk is above the target, it abstains to a broader run (rule-based uncertainty triggers are evaluated as an alternative). Layer~4 delivers the decision. Solid boxes have been implemented and evaluated in this paper; dashed boxes have been designed but not evaluated.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{7}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{eq:aci}{{6}{7}{}{}{}}
